Maintainer: Bernhard Haumacher <haui@haumacher.de>
Homepage: https://github.com/haumacher/valbum2
Depends: default-jre-headless (>= 2:1.21) | java21-runtime-headless | java22-runtime-headless | java23-runtime-headless | java24-runtime-headless | java25-runtime-headless | java-runtime-headless (>= 21), adduser
Suggests: openjdk-21-jre-headless
Description: Self-hosted photo and video album server
 VAlbum serves a folder tree of photos and videos as a private album: a JSON
 API plus the VAlbum web application, browsable from a phone, a tablet or a
 desktop, with users, groups, share links and invitations.
 .
 The originals are never modified, moved or deleted. Everything VAlbum stores
 about an album - titles, captions, ordering, ratings, privacy levels - lives
 in sidecar files beside the photos, so the folder tree stays the truth and can
 be copied away at any time.
 .
 The server runs as the system user "valbum" under systemd. Its configuration
 lives in /etc/default/valbum, its default library folder is /var/lib/valbum.
 That folder is never removed by the package, not even on purge.
